{"id": "EUVD-2026-25640", "enisaUuid": "176c501c-e021-385b-8d2d-f5cb5881c9f3", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\naf_unix: read UNIX_DIAG_VFS data under unix_state_lock\n\nExact UNIX diag lookups hold a reference to the socket, but not to\nu->path. Meanwhile, unix_release_sock() clears u->path under\nunix_state_lock() and drops the path reference after unlocking.\n\nRead the inode and device numbers for UNIX_DIAG_VFS while holding\nunix_state_lock(), then emit the netlink attribute after dropping the\nlock.\n\nThis keeps the VFS data stable while the reply is being built.", "datePublished": "2026-04-25T08:46:49", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T18:56:03", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e7339db13b9ddb63417b12da55fd6191e59f7442", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4f6a8f10182c3a9d22e8eb183957ae7ade9e4bf7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c3ec44ab4526bbc4b6c9fc845af86488244f4c9b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b9232421a77a649c9376c99fdfc8cb7f79cad34c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0c739f3785f84af695952c2bac8be2f45082c9b8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/900a4e0910e98b8caef117d5df00471fa438dcf9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bdf206e740bf2919d818f132c8c9cc7ed91d11c0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/39897df386376912d561d4946499379effa1e7ef"], "aliases": ["GHSA-pcr3-grpm-hh36", "CVE-2026-31673"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.14, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "006a3075-818a-370c-80eb-4cb9148dc42d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.175"}, {"id": "3a3630b1-51dd-3e29-af86-5854b8edfef2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.83"}, {"id": "3bf0d285-e644-3810-b136-c17d9a40c3b9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5f7b0569460b7d8d01ca776430a0050